00:43:29.250 --> 00:43:30.530
We gotta get this guy.

1031
00:43:30.650 --> 00:43:30.950
Yeah.

1032
00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:32.090
Yeah.

1033
00:43:32.310 --> 00:43:33.090
A real chair.

1034
00:43:33.450 --> 00:43:33.770
That is so funny.

1035
00:43:34.130 --> 00:43:35.490
It was delightful.

1036
00:43:35.970 --> 00:43:37.010
Great catch, Allison.

1037
00:43:38.050 --> 00:43:40.470
Andy has a new strategy for getting rid of Susan,

1038
00:43:40.470 --> 00:43:44.610
which is that he's gonna tell everyone in the bullpen to make it a miserable place to work,

1039
00:43:44.790 --> 00:43:47.090
so miserable that she wants to leave by lunch.

1040
00:43:48.150 --> 00:43:49.770
And, you know, Jim is gonna say,

1041
00:43:49.930 --> 00:43:52.890
I don't think we should try to make this place seem unpleasant.

1042
00:43:52.890 --> 00:43:56.290
I think we should just let this place crush her spirit by itself.

1043
00:43:56.330 --> 00:43:57.950
I mean, it knows what it's doing.

1044
00:43:58.170 --> 00:43:59.270
That made me laugh.

1045
00:43:59.490 --> 00:44:01.710
I also loved when Erin goes,

1046
00:44:01.850 --> 00:44:03.610
I know exactly what stapler to give her.

1047
00:44:03.710 --> 00:44:03.850
Yes.

1048
00:44:04.550 --> 00:44:06.330
And then we had the tiny one.

1049
00:44:06.690 --> 00:44:07.550
It's like so ridiculous.

1050
00:44:07.850 --> 00:44:09.170
That joke tastes so well.

1051
00:44:09.170 --> 00:44:12.690
No way, Ellie, like, as Erin placed it on the table, too.

1052
00:44:12.730 --> 00:44:12.990
Yeah.

1053
00:44:13.390 --> 00:44:14.990
Look what I've had to deal with.

1054
00:44:15.750 --> 00:44:18.410
Well, there was an alt-talking head for Jim,

1055
00:44:18.410 --> 00:44:23.210
and we find out a little something about Stanley that I want you all to hear.

1056
00:44:23.430 --> 00:44:23.730
Okay.

1057
00:44:24.370 --> 00:44:26.390
This whole thing is making me very uncomfortable.

1058
00:44:27.050 --> 00:44:28.950
I'm not getting in between the boss and his wife,

1059
00:44:29.030 --> 00:44:30.310
so just ask me about something else.

1060
00:44:31.370 --> 00:44:34.290
You know, Stanley's tie is really the story of the day.

1061
00:44:36.540 --> 00:44:37.680
It's my birthday.

1062
00:44:38.920 --> 00:44:42.410
Oh, it's been Stanley's birthday?

1063
00:44:42.710 --> 00:44:42.930
Yeah.

1064
00:44:44.880 --> 00:44:45.760
Where is his party?

1065
00:44:46.040 --> 00:44:48.240
What has happened to the party planning committee?

1066
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:51.840
And the best thing is when he says,

1067
00:44:52.100 --> 00:44:53.000
it is my birthday,

1068
00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:56.480
they do a full pan shot of his tie,

1069
00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:59.520
and his tie is a long blue fish,

1070
00:44:59.540 --> 00:45:02.320
and the face of it is the end of the tie.

1071
00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:02.720
Okay.

1072
00:45:03.160 --> 00:45:04.820
It is a hilarious tie.

1073
00:45:05.200 --> 00:45:07.980
He's clearly worn special for his birthday.

1074
00:45:08.680 --> 00:45:11.940
In the whole episode, I rewatched it looking for this tie.

1075
00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:13.540
You only see the top of it.

1076
00:45:13.760 --> 00:45:14.340
Oh, wow.

1077
00:45:14.340 --> 00:45:15.660
You just see the blue top.

1078
00:45:15.740 --> 00:45:18.000
But if it had ever shown him standing,

1079
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:20.000
you would have seen the fish face.

1080
00:45:20.780 --> 00:45:22.600
But it's Stanley's birthday.

1081
00:45:23.180 --> 00:45:24.800
Well, Pam is gone.

1082
00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:27.340
Maybe she was in charge of this.

1083
00:45:27.460 --> 00:45:28.100
But you know what?

1084
00:45:28.100 --> 00:45:29.560
What is Kathy for?

1085
00:45:29.920 --> 00:45:30.620
I don't know.

1086
00:45:30.760 --> 00:45:31.380
Pam is gone.

1087
00:45:31.500 --> 00:45:32.240
Angela's retired.

1088
00:45:32.400 --> 00:45:34.600
And Kathy is not doing her job.

1089
00:45:34.920 --> 00:45:37.040
No, not if Pam was in charge of birthday.

1090
00:45:37.040 --> 00:45:37.660
She's not.

1091
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.680
This is actually a good segue for me into the next scene.

1092
00:45:40.840 --> 00:45:42.180
We're in the break room,

1093
00:45:42.260 --> 00:45:44.100
and Oscar's passing around his phone

1094
00:45:44.100 --> 00:45:46.600
to kind of show everyone his, like, new puppy

1095
00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:49.180
who has crawled into a Williams-Sonoma ladle.

1096
00:45:49.460 --> 00:45:49.780
Gerald.

1097
00:45:50.220 --> 00:45:50.700
Yes.

1098
00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:53.100
And they're not letting Susan see the picture.

1099
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:55.200
They're kind of freezing her out of the conversation.

1100
00:45:56.000 --> 00:45:58.940
We got a fan question from a lot of people.

1101
00:45:59.180 --> 00:45:59.820
Gina S.

1102
00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:01.940
in Iowa, Meredith in Sacramento,

1103
00:46:02.360 --> 00:46:03.760
Lauren from Peoria, Illinois,

1104
00:46:04.240 --> 00:46:05.360
who all said,

1105
00:46:05.460 --> 00:46:08.180
Jenna had to leave the show temporarily for maternity leave,

1106
00:46:08.240 --> 00:46:09.380
but it has always bothered me

1107
00:46:09.380 --> 00:46:11.340
that Pam disappears with no fanfare.

1108
00:46:11.560 --> 00:46:13.960
It seems like Jim would have been more excited

1109
00:46:13.960 --> 00:46:16.000
to share the birth of their second child

1110
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.460
or the story of the delivery

1111
00:46:18.460 --> 00:46:20.840
or maybe how mom and baby are doing.

1112
00:46:21.020 --> 00:46:21.480
Something.

1113
00:46:21.660 --> 00:46:22.460
There's nothing.

1114
00:46:22.880 --> 00:46:24.500
Was there a writing decision

1115
00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:26.740
to not focus on this part of their lives?

1116
00:46:26.740 --> 00:46:28.520
I really would have loved to see more of Jim

1117
00:46:28.520 --> 00:46:31.420
acknowledging the addition to his family in this episode.

1118
00:46:31.700 --> 00:46:32.680
Well, first of all,

1119
00:46:32.860 --> 00:46:35.080
Steve Burgess reminded me that my son was born

1120
00:46:35.080 --> 00:46:37.840
the Saturday before we started filming this episode.

1121
00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:38.460
Aw.

1122
00:46:38.780 --> 00:46:39.140
Yeah.

1123
00:46:39.580 --> 00:46:41.580
And as I was watching this episode,

1124
00:46:41.780 --> 00:46:43.140
I, too, was surprised

1125
00:46:43.140 --> 00:46:45.260
that Pam had given birth

1126
00:46:45.260 --> 00:46:46.900
and we do not mention it at all,

1127
00:46:46.940 --> 00:46:48.900
so I asked Charlie Grandy about it.

1128
00:46:48.980 --> 00:46:50.020
He was the director of this episode,

1129
00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:51.180
but he's a longtime writer.

1130
00:46:51.500 --> 00:46:52.900
And Charlie said this,

1131
00:46:53.000 --> 00:46:55.400
It is weird that we spend more time

1132
00:46:55.400 --> 00:46:57.540
learning about Oscar's dog in a ladle

1133
00:46:57.540 --> 00:46:58.740
than Jim and Pam's baby.

1134
00:46:58.880 --> 00:47:00.780
I can't remember what the thinking was,

1135
00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:02.320
but being a second child myself,

1136
00:47:02.320 --> 00:47:03.800
I can attest to the fact

1137
00:47:03.800 --> 00:47:06.000
that we just don't get the same amount of attention.

1138
00:47:06.560 --> 00:47:09.080
All we can hope is that the second child of theirs

1139
00:47:09.080 --> 00:47:11.540
is now 12 and turning toward comedy

1140
00:47:11.540 --> 00:47:13.520
as a desperate way to finally be seen.

1141
00:47:13.700 --> 00:47:13.860
Aw.

1142
00:47:15.140 --> 00:47:17.720
You know, there was also an Aaron talking head

1143
00:47:17.720 --> 00:47:19.660
that would have followed this scene

1144
00:47:19.660 --> 00:47:21.760
that is absolutely delicious.

1145
00:47:22.120 --> 00:47:23.880
I saw it in the shooting draft.

1146
00:47:24.220 --> 00:47:25.540
She is really struggling

1147
00:47:25.540 --> 00:47:27.980
with the fact that they were freezing Susan

1148
00:47:27.980 --> 00:47:29.180
out of this conversation.

1149
00:47:29.240 --> 00:47:30.760
And here's what she would have said.

1150
00:47:30.840 --> 00:47:31.480
It made me laugh.

1151
00:47:31.780 --> 00:47:34.560
You don't keep a puppy picture from a nice lady.

1152
00:47:34.740 --> 00:47:35.720
I feel sick.

1153
00:47:36.180 --> 00:47:38.020
And it was that type of ladle.

1154
00:47:38.380 --> 00:47:39.240
There you go.

1155
00:47:40.760 --> 00:47:43.040
I just like it that you don't keep a puppy picture

1156
00:47:43.040 --> 00:47:43.960
from a nice lady.

1157
00:47:44.380 --> 00:47:46.420
Yeah, I think the whole office was struggling

1158
00:47:46.420 --> 00:47:47.380
because they liked her.

1159
00:47:47.640 --> 00:47:49.580
Andy had a talking head that was in the shooting draft

1160
00:47:49.580 --> 00:47:50.700
that didn't make it where he said,

1161
00:47:50.820 --> 00:47:53.680
please, please, just somebody piss off the nice lady.

1162
00:47:53.980 --> 00:47:54.380
Yes.

1163
00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:55.380
Exactly.

1164
00:47:56.340 --> 00:47:58.160
Well, Susan's going to have a talking head

1165
00:47:58.160 --> 00:47:59.260
where she says, you know what?

1166
00:47:59.260 --> 00:47:59.980
I get it.

1167
00:48:00.120 --> 00:48:01.280
The last time I had a job,

1168
00:48:01.380 --> 00:48:02.840
I hated the boss's wife, too.

1169
00:48:03.440 --> 00:48:05.260
Of course, she was married to Robert.

1170
00:48:06.600 --> 00:48:07.060
Wow.

1171
00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:09.580
Susan, a little scandalous.

1172
00:48:10.280 --> 00:48:12.460
Now she's going to go confide to her husband

1173
00:48:13.100 --> 00:48:15.940
that she doesn't think anyone here really likes her.

1174
00:48:16.620 --> 00:48:19.460
He's like, we will do something about this right away.

1175
00:48:19.960 --> 00:48:22.040
Again, Robert, you're overselling.

1176
00:48:22.240 --> 00:48:23.340
You're overselling this.

1177
00:48:23.460 --> 00:48:24.760
He's like, Andy, get in here.

1178
00:48:24.980 --> 00:48:26.880
And then he excuses himself.

1179
00:48:27.040 --> 00:48:29.100
He's like, not going to stick around for the conversation.

1180
00:48:29.340 --> 00:48:30.500
Andy, fix it.

1181
00:48:30.680 --> 00:48:33.360
And Susan is going to get Andy to reveal

1182
00:48:34.120 --> 00:48:38.700
that maybe, maybe there's something more going on here.

1183
00:48:38.900 --> 00:48:40.760
Andy is no match for Susan.

1184
00:48:40.960 --> 00:48:41.200
No.

1185
00:48:41.380 --> 00:48:44.320
She is just watching him and observing quietly

1186
00:48:44.320 --> 00:48:46.160
and figuring it all out.

1187
00:48:46.800 --> 00:48:49.560
And Andy cannot hide his truth.

1188
00:48:50.040 --> 00:48:52.280
We're going to get our first glimpse now

1189
00:48:52.280 --> 00:48:56.080
of Dwight's newfangled gym with all the real equipment.

1190
00:48:56.340 --> 00:48:58.640
His gym for muscles is really nice.

1191
00:48:58.880 --> 00:49:00.680
I remember this gym.

1192
00:49:01.280 --> 00:49:03.920
At one point, I remember the writers got a treadmill.

1193
00:49:04.100 --> 00:49:05.080
I remember that.

1194
00:49:05.220 --> 00:49:06.580
It was in their writer's trailer.

1195
00:49:06.780 --> 00:49:09.200
And I would go in there and I would walk on that treadmill.

1196
00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:10.020
Me too.

1197
00:49:10.300 --> 00:49:12.620
The treadmill that you see in Dwight's gym

1198
00:49:12.620 --> 00:49:14.780
is the one, they took it from the writer's trailer.

1199
00:49:15.160 --> 00:49:18.200
Steve Burgess said, yeah, that was the writer's trailer treadmill.

1200
00:49:18.560 --> 00:49:21.900
And after this episode, we got to keep almost all of that equipment.

1201
00:49:22.040 --> 00:49:24.000
And we finally had a gym.

1202
00:49:24.680 --> 00:49:28.720
Dwight's gym for muscles became the cast and crew gym.

1203
00:49:29.220 --> 00:49:30.760
Finally, after eight years.

1204
00:49:31.220 --> 00:49:32.760
I never used it a single time.

1205
00:49:32.860 --> 00:49:33.620
Did you ever use it?

1206
00:49:33.900 --> 00:49:34.360
Yes.

1207
00:49:34.540 --> 00:49:34.720
You did?

1208
00:49:34.720 --> 00:49:36.640
I used to walk on the treadmill all the time.

1209
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:38.140
No, I walked on the treadmill.

1210
00:49:38.200 --> 00:49:40.460
But all the weights and all that stuff.

1211
00:49:40.460 --> 00:49:41.340
I used the weights.

1212
00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:41.800
You did?

1213
00:49:41.960 --> 00:49:42.400
I did.

1214
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:44.020
Yeah, because I do like weights.

1215
00:49:44.220 --> 00:49:45.340
Yeah, I didn't do any of that.

1216
00:49:45.880 --> 00:49:49.460
I did love Dwight trying to motivate Daryl to work out.

1217
00:49:49.820 --> 00:49:52.840
And Daryl was like, I was just on the treadmill for 35 minutes.

1218
00:49:52.860 --> 00:49:54.420
And Dwight goes, no, you weren't.

1219
00:49:54.480 --> 00:49:55.000
I timed it.

1220
00:49:55.120 --> 00:49:55.920
It was eight minutes.

1221
00:49:56.860 --> 00:49:58.400
That rang so true to me.

1222
00:49:58.480 --> 00:50:00.520
Because I feel like I get on the treadmill for five minutes.

1223
00:50:00.520 --> 00:50:01.400
I'm like, oh my God.

1224
00:50:01.680 --> 00:50:02.880
I've been here forever.

1225
00:50:03.080 --> 00:50:03.440
Yeah.

1226
00:50:03.440 --> 00:50:08.440
Yeah, I really wish like podcasts were around back then because I feel like I would have

1227
00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:10.800
worked out so much more if I could have listened to a podcaSt.

1228
00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:12.280
I used to have like playlists.

1229
00:50:12.400 --> 00:50:12.560
Yeah.

1230
00:50:13.300 --> 00:50:14.060
Oh my gosh.

1231
00:50:14.160 --> 00:50:16.460
Do you think anyone is working out right now?

1232
00:50:16.460 --> 00:50:18.840
Are we keeping you company on a treadmill somewhere?

1233
00:50:19.420 --> 00:50:22.820
If you are working out right now, you can do it.

1234
00:50:22.960 --> 00:50:23.960
You got it.

1235
00:50:24.120 --> 00:50:24.800
Keep going.

1236
00:50:25.140 --> 00:50:25.600
Yes.

1237
00:50:25.720 --> 00:50:31.420
And in the words of Dwight from this episode, bring that same buffalo wing passion to this gym.

1238
00:50:31.520 --> 00:50:32.740
You can do it.

1239
00:50:32.740 --> 00:50:33.600
That's right.

1240
00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:35.100
You're getting healthy.

1241
00:50:35.460 --> 00:50:36.120
Way to go.

1242
00:50:37.060 --> 00:50:38.140
That was a good little pep talk.

1243
00:50:38.200 --> 00:50:38.880
That was pep talk.

1244
00:50:39.060 --> 00:50:39.440
All right.

1245
00:50:40.080 --> 00:50:44.340
Well, Robert is going to return and he finds Andy and Susan still in the conference room.

1246
00:50:44.500 --> 00:50:46.500
And Susan's going to say, hey, you know what?

1247
00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:49.140
Turns out I'm not going to be working here after all.

1248
00:50:49.840 --> 00:50:51.840
And then she basically says, you know what?

1249
00:50:52.320 --> 00:50:53.960
Andy kind of let me in on it.

1250
00:50:54.320 --> 00:50:55.340
I'm up to speed.

1251
00:50:55.500 --> 00:50:57.680
And Robert's like, what are you talking about?

1252
00:50:57.980 --> 00:50:58.540
You know?

1253
00:50:58.720 --> 00:51:02.140
And Andy says, hey, I don't want to get caught in the middle of this marital issue.

1254
00:51:02.140 --> 00:51:05.160
And Robert's like, Andy, be honest, okay?

1255
00:51:05.460 --> 00:51:09.960
Whatever you're trying to do right now, Andy, whatever this privacy thing is you're trying

1256
00:51:09.960 --> 00:51:11.500
to do, we don't need it.

1257
00:51:11.600 --> 00:51:12.640
Just be honeSt.

1258
00:51:13.900 --> 00:51:14.860
No games.

1259
00:51:15.420 --> 00:51:17.080
And Andy's like, no games?

1260
00:51:17.880 --> 00:51:18.800
No games.

1261
00:51:18.980 --> 00:51:19.640
Be honeSt.

1262
00:51:19.900 --> 00:51:22.640
So Andy's like, okay, here's everything that happened.

1263
00:51:22.800 --> 00:51:23.720
He came running in.

1264
00:51:23.840 --> 00:51:24.440
He banged on the window.

1265
00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:25.640
He said, don't give her a job.

1266
00:51:25.760 --> 00:51:26.100
Blah, blah, blah.

1267
00:51:26.800 --> 00:51:29.920
And Robert's like, you son of a bitch.

1268
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:30.940
You liar.

1269
00:51:31.260 --> 00:51:32.420
You are a liar.

1270
00:51:32.980 --> 00:51:34.180
Say you're lying.

1271
00:51:35.120 --> 00:51:40.180
So Andy's like, listen, the person who knows everything, who was there when it happened

1272
00:51:40.180 --> 00:51:40.720
is Jim.

1273
00:51:40.960 --> 00:51:42.320
Jim knows the whole truth.

1274
00:51:42.640 --> 00:51:46.720
Well, Jim hears this, and he has to get out of Dodge.

1275
00:51:46.980 --> 00:51:49.680
It made me laugh when Robert goes, wait, where's Jim?

1276
00:51:49.760 --> 00:51:52.360
And Aaron goes, he like crawled out.

1277
00:51:52.520 --> 00:51:54.700
He like rolled and then crawled and scooched.

1278
00:51:55.360 --> 00:52:00.540
So Charlie Grandy said that they really needed something new for this storyline to happen

1279
00:52:00.540 --> 00:52:01.220
in Act 3.

1280
00:52:01.520 --> 00:52:06.120
So they came up with this storyline of Jim needing to escape.

1281
00:52:06.460 --> 00:52:10.960
They thought it would be a really great way to inject some kind of silly physical comedy

1282
00:52:10.960 --> 00:52:13.820
into the script and also relieve some of the tension.

1283
00:52:14.060 --> 00:52:14.240
Yeah.

1284
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:18.120
Because now they're going to have to go as a group and find Jim.

1285
00:52:18.380 --> 00:52:22.060
I loved when he dropped his shoe as he was climbing up the side of the building, and

1286
00:52:22.060 --> 00:52:23.740
he goes, ow, ow, ow.

1287
00:52:23.740 --> 00:52:27.640
Because you know that little metal bar on your bare foot climbing would hurt.

1288
00:52:27.960 --> 00:52:28.260
Yes.

1289
00:52:28.480 --> 00:52:33.620
We got a fan question from Maddie in Arkansas who said, did Jim really climb that ladder

1290
00:52:33.620 --> 00:52:34.700
to the top of the building?

1291
00:52:34.960 --> 00:52:39.040
It feels like a major stunt that would definitely require a safety meeting.

1292
00:52:39.420 --> 00:52:42.200
Also, how did they make his shoe fall off just right?

1293
00:52:42.820 --> 00:52:47.320
Well, Charlie Grandy said that shooting Jim on the ladder and then on the roof was absolutely

1294
00:52:47.320 --> 00:52:51.280
nerve-wracking, especially on the ladder and when he had to drop the shoe because he did

1295
00:52:51.280 --> 00:52:52.740
not think that John was harnessed in.

1296
00:52:52.740 --> 00:52:54.840
He does not look harnessed in.

1297
00:52:55.020 --> 00:52:57.280
He looks like he's just climbing the ladder.

1298
00:52:57.660 --> 00:53:03.680
Steve Burgess said that he thinks we did have a safety harness on John and we removed the

1299
00:53:03.680 --> 00:53:04.800
wire in poSt.

1300
00:53:05.240 --> 00:53:06.940
Well, let's stick with that story.

1301
00:53:08.160 --> 00:53:12.220
And Steve said, we did have several safety meetings about it.

1302
00:53:12.380 --> 00:53:14.880
We had just changed stunt coordinators.

1303
00:53:15.100 --> 00:53:18.160
Our new stunt coordinator was Brett Jones, starting with this episode.

1304
00:53:18.400 --> 00:53:20.740
And the whole shoe thing was just John.

1305
00:53:20.740 --> 00:53:24.340
He just kicked it off and it was perfect and we only had to do one take.

1306
00:53:24.520 --> 00:53:26.840
He said John was completely safe the whole time.

1307
00:53:26.840 --> 00:53:29.020
It just looked a lot more dangerous than it really was.

1308
00:53:29.320 --> 00:53:29.460
Okay.

1309
00:53:29.880 --> 00:53:30.220
Okay.

1310
00:53:30.400 --> 00:53:30.780
Okay.

1311
00:53:31.420 --> 00:53:34.120
Well, you know, when Jim gets to the roof, Creed is up there.

1312
00:53:34.380 --> 00:53:36.080
Yeah, he's flying his helicopter.

1313
00:53:36.480 --> 00:53:39.620
We had a fan question from Brent D in Virginia.

1314
00:53:40.080 --> 00:53:45.580
In a webisode from three years earlier, Creed was shown shopping for a helicopter on his work

1315
00:53:45.580 --> 00:53:52.260
He had blackmailed his co-workers for the funds and supposedly he was going to, quote,

1316
00:53:52.500 --> 00:53:57.360
fly it down to Brazil, down to the Amazon in search of the world's largest bookstore.

1317
00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:03.520
Brett said, on its own and without any prior setup, Creed's rooftop pastime just seems like

1318
00:54:03.520 --> 00:54:05.980
another one of his many quirky eccentricities.

1319
00:54:06.440 --> 00:54:10.920
Was that the intent or was this a callback on the writer's part?

1320
00:54:10.920 --> 00:54:17.640
Brett, this was an amazing callback and I love that you spotted it.

1321
00:54:17.860 --> 00:54:19.380
Yeah, great catch.

1322
00:54:19.900 --> 00:54:22.440
I guess Dwight's a personal trainer now.

1323
00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:25.680
Apparently, he's going to show you how to do a pelvic bowl.

1324
00:54:26.580 --> 00:54:29.320
Daryl's not into it, but Gabe right away is like, hey, nice pelvic bowl.

1325
00:54:30.200 --> 00:54:33.180
So like I said, the gym storyline is a lot bigger.

1326
00:54:33.580 --> 00:54:37.640
Here are the office co-workers that join Dwight's Gym for Muscles.

1327
00:54:37.640 --> 00:54:42.480
In addition to Daryl, Kathy, Aaron, Oscar, Gabe, and Meredith all join.

1328
00:54:42.700 --> 00:54:44.260
And you see them working out.

1329
00:54:44.300 --> 00:54:44.620
Oh, yeah.

1330
00:54:44.740 --> 00:54:46.180
There's some really funny scenes.

1331
00:54:46.500 --> 00:54:51.760
And as it turns out, you know, we find out why Daryl wants to be at the gym.

1332
00:54:51.840 --> 00:54:54.840
He finally admits he wants to look good for Val.

1333
00:54:55.100 --> 00:54:55.400
Yes.

1334
00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:57.440
Of course, Dwight thinks this is Val Kilmer.

1335
00:54:58.080 --> 00:55:02.900
Well, you know, we had a really great fan catch from Jenny B in Ontario, Canada, who says,

1336
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:06.620
is it just me or is Gabe running backwards on the elliptical machine?

1337
00:55:07.200 --> 00:55:08.600
Yes, he is.

1338
00:55:09.000 --> 00:55:12.460
I looked at his feet, and he's going in the reverse order.

1339
00:55:12.660 --> 00:55:13.440
He's not going forward.

1340
00:55:13.600 --> 00:55:14.380
He's going backwards.

1341
00:55:14.960 --> 00:55:18.240
Well, Susan and Robert's storyline is going to wrap up back in the conference room.

1342
00:55:18.340 --> 00:55:19.960
They're now in there with Andy and Jim.

1343
00:55:20.140 --> 00:55:23.700
And Susan very pointedly says to Jim, is this all true?

1344
00:55:23.920 --> 00:55:25.500
Does Robert not want me to work here?

1345
00:55:25.680 --> 00:55:26.560
Answer the question.

1346
00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:30.320
And Jim kind of gives a long speech about how he works with his wife.

1347
00:55:30.320 --> 00:55:31.940
And he loves working with his wife.

1348
00:55:31.960 --> 00:55:33.760
And he wishes she were here.

1349
00:55:33.760 --> 00:55:41.000
And the more he talks, the more apparent it is how true that is for Jim and how untrue

1350
00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:42.040
it is for Robert.

1351
00:55:42.700 --> 00:55:42.960
Yes.

1352
00:55:43.200 --> 00:55:48.900
We don't see exactly how Robert and Susan are going to resolve this within their marriage,

1353
00:55:48.900 --> 00:55:51.440
but it is clear that Susan is not going to work there.

1354
00:55:51.440 --> 00:55:57.320
And she goes down to the parking lot with Andy, and then she sort of hits on him?

1355
00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:58.440
Not sort of.

1356
00:55:58.720 --> 00:56:02.900
To me, it implied that she doesn't think things with Robert are working out,

1357
00:56:02.900 --> 00:56:06.440
because she says when all of this settles down, it's a date.

1358
00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:07.220
Yeah.

1359
00:56:07.520 --> 00:56:09.260
We really hit it off, I think.

1360
00:56:09.440 --> 00:56:09.780
Yeah.

1361
00:56:10.800 --> 00:56:11.980
Fan mail flurry.

1362
00:56:12.220 --> 00:56:12.740
I bet.

1363
00:56:12.740 --> 00:56:18.600
But people wanted to know, was there any plan to continue the Andy, Mrs. California storyline?

1364
00:56:19.200 --> 00:56:25.180
Well, Charlie Grandy said he thinks there was, but he's not really sure what happened

1365
00:56:25.180 --> 00:56:30.580
to that arc, because he had to leave the office immediately after shooting this episode.

1366
00:56:30.820 --> 00:56:35.460
He said that while we were shooting the Act 2 conference room scene with Andy, Susan,

1367
00:56:35.460 --> 00:56:40.220
and Robert, he got a phone call, and he learned that a pilot he had written was going to get

1368
